---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import {
  repoUrl,
  issuesUrl,
  discussionsUrl,
  contactEmail,
} from "../site";
---

<Base
  title="Contribute"
  description="How to help LibreDental: contribute code, share feedback as a dental professional, spread the word, or endorse the project."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Contribute</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      LibreDental is built by volunteers. What helps most right now is people:
      users, contributors and word of mouth.
    </p>

    <div class="notice">
      <p class="notice-title">About donations</p>
      <p>
        Donations are always appreciated, but we haven't set up a way to
        donate yet, and the project is in a good place right now. If you'd like
        to help, the options below make the biggest difference.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Spread the word</h2>
    <p>
      This is the single most helpful thing you can do. Know a developer who'd
      enjoy the project, or a dentist tired of locked-in software? Tell them
      about LibreDental. Mention it to colleagues, in study clubs, on forums or
      on social media. Every new user and contributor makes the project
      stronger.
    </p>

    <h2>Developers</h2>
    <p>
      Code, testing, packaging and documentation are all welcome. LibreDental
      is in early alpha, so there's plenty to work on and your contributions
      can shape how it turns out.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Start with the <a href={repoUrl}>source code on GitHub</a>; the README
        includes the contribution guide.
      </li>
      <li>
        Browse the <a href={issuesUrl}>open issues</a> to find something to pick
        up, or report bugs you run into.
      </li>
      <li>
        Not sure where to start? Ask in
        <a href={discussionsUrl}>Discussions</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Dentists and dental staff</h2>
    <p>
      Software for dental offices should be shaped by the people who work in
      them. If you're a dentist, hygienist, assistant or office manager, your
      feedback is some of the most valuable help we can get.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="/download/">Try LibreDental with demo data</a> and tell us
        what's missing, confusing or wrong for how your practice actually works.
      </li>
      <li>
        Share your workflows for charting, scheduling, billing and insurance,
        so we build the things that matter first.
      </li>
      <li>
        Post in <a href={discussionsUrl}>Discussions</a> or email
        <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. No technical
        knowledge needed.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sponsorship and endorsement</h2>
    <p>
      If you're a practice, dental school, professional association or company
      that believes dental software should be free and open, a public
      endorsement helps other practices trust the project and helps us find
      contributors. We're always happy to hear from organisations that want to
      be involved.
    </p>
    <p>
      Get in touch at
      <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
